# Line endings, decided here rather than left to each machine's Git setting.
#
# The files that run on the relay laptops must reach them with Windows line
# endings. A .cmd with Unix endings is read by cmd.exe a line at a time and can
# be misparsed - the batch files do their work inside one block for the same
# reason - and PowerShell and WSH files are happier the same way. Until now
# they were stored with Unix endings and only became Windows ones because Git
# for Windows was set to convert them; a machine without that setting, or a
# download straight from GitHub, got the Unix version.
#
# Everything else is normalised to Unix endings in the repository, whatever the
# working copy looks like, so a diff never turns into "every line changed".

* text=auto eol=lf

*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
